<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto p-4 space-y-8">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-parchment">Science Pipeline</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-sm flex-1">
        Run the food-science pipeline end to end. Each stage feeds the next:
        discover papers (per food species, by its curated scientific name) →
        extract compounds → derive & promote ingredient↔compound facts (which then
        feed back as targeted crawl terms). Progress updates live as batches run. See <code class="text-parchment">docs/scientific_pipeline.md</code>.
      </p>
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="refresh"
        class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-ink-panel2 text-parchment text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90"
      >
        Refresh
      </button>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-ink-panel2 bg-ink-panel p-4">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink-panel2 text-parchment text-xs font-semibold">
          1
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-parchment mr-2">
          Paper discovery (Entrez/PubMed crawl)
        </h2>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="run_crawl"
          disabled={running?(@crawl_run)}
          data-confirm="Crawl PubMed for every food species with a curated scientific name? This calls the NCBI API and can be long-running."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded bg-basil text-ink text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          {if running?(@crawl_run), do: "Crawling…", else: "Run crawl"}
        </button>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="reset_crawl"
          disabled={running?(@crawl_run)}
          data-confirm="Reset the crawl? This deletes ALL discovered studies and everything downstream — entity annotations, full-texts, measurement candidates, and derived candidates. Curated species, the compound registry, and relationships are kept. This cannot be undone."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-red-500/40 text-red-300 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-red-500/10 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          Reset
        </button>

        <.link
          navigate={~p"/professional/science/studies"}
          class="text-sm text-basil hover:underline ml-auto"
        >
          Review studies →
        </.link>
      </div>

      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-xs">
        Finds research papers for each food species (by its curated scientific
        name) against its linked compounds and phytochemistry keywords, linking
        each paper to every ingredient curated onto that species.
      </p>

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-parchment-dim mb-1">
          <span>
            Processed: {@crawl_progress.processed} / {@crawl_progress.total} ({percent(
              @crawl_progress
            )}%)
          </span>
          <span class={"font-medium #{run_class(@crawl_run)}"} title={run_error(@crawl_run)}>
            {run_label(@crawl_run)}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="h-2 w-full rounded bg-ink-panel2 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-full bg-basil rounded" style={"width: #{percent(@crawl_progress)}%"}>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-ink-panel2 bg-ink-panel p-4">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink-panel2 text-parchment text-xs font-semibold">
          2
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-parchment mr-2">Entity annotation (PubTator3)</h2>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="run_annotation"
          disabled={running?(@annotation_run)}
          data-confirm="Annotate every discovered study via PubTator3? This calls the NCBI API and can be long-running."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded bg-basil text-ink text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          {if running?(@annotation_run), do: "Annotating…", else: "Run annotation"}
        </button>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="reset_annotation"
          disabled={running?(@annotation_run)}
          data-confirm="Reset annotation? This deletes all PubTator entity mentions and the annotation cache/ledger so annotation can re-run. Discovered studies are kept."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-red-500/40 text-red-300 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-red-500/10 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          Reset
        </button>

        <.link
          navigate={~p"/professional/science/entities"}
          class="text-sm text-basil hover:underline ml-auto"
        >
          Review entities →
        </.link>
      </div>

      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-xs">
        Extracts chemicals, species and diseases from each study. Chemicals resolve
        into the compound registry — this is where compounds appear.
      </p>

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-parchment-dim mb-1">
          <span>
            Processed: {@annotation_progress.processed} / {@annotation_progress.total} ({percent(
              @annotation_progress
            )}%)
          </span>
          <span
            class={"font-medium #{run_class(@annotation_run)}"}
            title={run_error(@annotation_run)}
          >
            {run_label(@annotation_run)}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="h-2 w-full rounded bg-ink-panel2 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-full bg-basil rounded" style={"width: #{percent(@annotation_progress)}%"}>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-ink-panel2 bg-ink-panel p-4">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink-panel2 text-parchment text-xs font-semibold">
          4
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-parchment mr-2">Candidate derivation</h2>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="derive"
          disabled={running?(@derivation_run)}
          data-confirm="Derive candidates from all current evidence and auto-promote strong ones?"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded bg-basil text-ink text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          {if running?(@derivation_run), do: "Deriving…", else: "Derive candidates"}
        </button>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="reset_derivation"
          disabled={running?(@derivation_run)}
          data-confirm="Reset derivation? This deletes all derived candidates, their study citations, and derivation runs, plus the auto-promoted 'contains' facts. Manually-curated relationships are kept."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-red-500/40 text-red-300 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-red-500/10 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          Reset
        </button>

        <.link
          navigate={~p"/professional/compound-candidates"}
          class="text-sm text-basil hover:underline ml-auto"
        >
          Review candidates & facts →
        </.link>
      </div>

      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-xs">
        Scores ingredient↔compound pairs from co-occurrence and measurements.
        Strong evidence auto-promotes into curated facts; the rest waits for review below.
      </p>

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-parchment-dim mb-1">
          <span>
            Derived: {@derivation_progress.processed} / {@derivation_progress.total} ({percent(
              @derivation_progress
            )}%)
          </span>
          <span
            class={"font-medium #{run_class(@derivation_run)}"}
            title={run_error(@derivation_run)}
          >
            {run_label(@derivation_run)}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="h-2 w-full rounded bg-ink-panel2 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-full bg-basil rounded" style={"width: #{percent(@derivation_progress)}%"}>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-ink-panel2 bg-ink-panel p-4">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink-panel2 text-parchment text-xs font-semibold">
          5
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-parchment mr-2">Recommendation derivation (disease → compound)</h2>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="derive_recommendations"
          disabled={running?(@recommendation_run)}
          data-confirm="Derive condition↔compound recommendation candidates from the directional literature relations already on disk? These are review-gated — nothing is auto-promoted."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded bg-basil text-ink text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          {if running?(@recommendation_run), do: "Deriving…", else: "Derive recommendations"}
        </button>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="reset_recommendations"
          disabled={running?(@recommendation_run)}
          data-confirm="Reset recommendation derivation? This deletes all derived recommendation candidates, their citations, and derivation runs. Curated health recommendations and the underlying relations are kept."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-red-500/40 text-red-300 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-red-500/10 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          Reset
        </button>

        <.link
          navigate={~p"/professional/health"}
          class="text-sm text-basil hover:underline ml-auto"
        >
          Review recommendations →
        </.link>
      </div>

      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-xs">
        Aggregates PubTator's directional chemical↔disease relations (negative → lean
        <span class="font-medium">encourage</span>, positive → lean
        <span class="font-medium">avoid</span>) into scored, review-gated candidates.
        An admin confirms direction & severity to promote into a curated
        <code class="text-parchment">Health.CompoundRecommendation</code> — never auto-promoted.
      </p>

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-parchment-dim mb-1">
          <span>
            Derived: {@recommendation_progress.processed} / {@recommendation_progress.total} ({percent(
              @recommendation_progress
            )}%)
          </span>
          <span
            class={"font-medium #{run_class(@recommendation_run)}"}
            title={run_error(@recommendation_run)}
          >
            {run_label(@recommendation_run)}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="h-2 w-full rounded bg-ink-panel2 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-full bg-basil rounded" style={"width: #{percent(@recommendation_progress)}%"}>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%!-- ── Full-text (PMC) + measurement extraction (external local-AI service) ── --%>
    <section class="space-y-3 rounded-lg border border-ink-panel2 bg-ink-panel p-4">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-ink-panel2 text-parchment text-xs font-semibold">
          FT
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-parchment mr-2">Full-text extraction (measurements)</h2>

        <button
          type="button"
          phx-click="reset_extraction"
          data-confirm="Reset extraction? This deletes all PMC full-texts, fetch attempts, and extracted measurement candidates so the local-AI service re-processes every study from scratch. Discovered studies and accepted measurements are kept."
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-red-500/40 text-red-300 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-red-500/10 disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        >
          Reset
        </button>

        <span class="font-medium text-sm ml-auto text-parchment-dim">External · local-AI service</span>
      </div>

      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-xs">
        PMC open-access full text + compound-measurement extraction (Bumblebee QA) runs off-box in the
        <code class="text-parchment">mehungry_local_ai</code> service and posts candidates back over REST
        (<code class="text-parchment">mix local_ai.extract</code>). This panel is read-only status.
      </p>

      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-parchment-dim mb-1">
          <span>PMC fetched: {@pmc_progress.processed} / {@pmc_progress.total} ({percent(@pmc_progress)}%)</span>
          <span>
            <.link navigate={~p"/professional/compound-candidates"} class="text-basil hover:underline">{@mcand_count} pending review →</.link>
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="h-2 w-full rounded bg-ink-panel2 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-full bg-basil rounded" style={"width: #{percent(@pmc_progress)}%"}></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-medium text-parchment mb-2">Pending review</h2>
      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-sm mb-3">
        Strongest evidence first. <span class="font-medium">Promote</span>
        writes a curated relationship; <span class="font-medium">Reject</span>
        drops it. Both leave the queue.
      </p>

      <div
        id="science_pipeline_candidates"
        phx-hook="InfiniteScroll"
        phx-update="stream"
        data-page={@page}
        class="divide-y divide-ink-panel2"
      >
        <div
          :for={{dom_id, candidate} <- @streams.candidates}
          id={dom_id}
          class="py-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 justify-between"
        >
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <div class="text-parchment font-medium truncate">
              {candidate.species.name} <span class="text-parchment-dim">contains</span>
              {candidate.compound.name}
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-parchment-dim">
              evidence:
              <span class={"font-medium #{level_class(candidate.evidence_level)}"}>
                {candidate.evidence_level || "insufficient"}
              </span>
              · score: {score_label(candidate.evidence_score)} · {candidate.study_count} lit · {candidate.measurement_study_count} meas
              · sources: {(candidate.sources || []) |> Enum.join(", ")}
            </div>
            <div :if={candidate.studies != []} class="text-xs text-parchment-dim mt-0.5">
              refs:
              <a
                :for={study <- candidate.studies}
                href={"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/#{study.pmid}/"}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                class="text-basil hover:underline mr-1"
              >{study.pmid}</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <button
              type="button"
              phx-click="promote"
              phx-value-id={candidate.id}
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded bg-basil text-ink text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90"
            >
              Promote
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              phx-click="reject"
              phx-value-id={candidate.id}
              data-confirm="Reject this candidate? It will not be promoted."
              class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-ink-panel2 text-parchment text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90"
            >
              Reject
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-parchment-dim text-sm mt-4">
        Scroll to load more. Promoted and rejected rows leave this list.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-parchment-dim text-xs border-t border-ink-panel2 pt-4">
      Not shown here: recording quantitative measurements (step 3) and reading
      evidence summaries / health advice (steps 6–7) are data & read concerns, not
      run-buttons — see <code class="text-parchment">docs/scientific_pipeline.md</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
